{"parentUuid":"730d53f4-3236-43e1-a6ef-e7c77712c611","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/harborlight","sessionId":"planted-01","version":"2.0.21","gitBranch":"fix/queue-test","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_01lv71z3u0l6gjIZHNkFCZTY","content":"src/queue.ts:31:  /** Resolves when the queue is empty and no flush is in flight. */\nsrc/queue.ts:32:  drained(): Promise<void> {\nsrc/queue.ts:44:  private inFlight = 0;\nsrc/queue.ts:52:    this.inFlight++;\nsrc/queue.ts:58:    this.inFlight--;\nsrc/shutdown.ts:12:  await queue.drained();"}]},"uuid":"e5b64263-2f3f-420e-a062-c837dabdfe1d","timestamp":"2026-09-25T19:16:13.000Z"}
{"parentUuid":"e5b64263-2f3f-420e-a062-c837dabdfe1d","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/harborlight","sessionId":"planted-01","version":"2.0.21","gitBranch":"fix/queue-test","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01Q81CypgD7VsVk5NCEtIIVK","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The test pushes 20 items, which fills the batch and flushes immediately, and then sleeps a fixed 100 ms before asserting the queue is empty. But FakeSink.write takes a random 20 to 120 ms, so about one run in five the write is still in flight at 100 ms and size() is not zero yet. That matches 'one in six'. The queue already has drained(), which resolves when it is empty and nothing is in flight, and shutdown.ts uses it. Let me check what the testing docs recommend before I change the pattern."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":241,"output_tokens":265}},"uuid":"708858a5-979d-41c7-a835-1d9b56239ecc","timestamp":"2026-09-25T19:16:21.000Z","requestId":"req_011C39pEj55c9tjyqRSLlyEd"}
